# RTX 5090 32GB (Blackwell / SM 12.0) — verified on a rented vast.ai 5090 +
# Ryzen 9 9950X, and the target profile for a local 5090 demo box.
#
# Same community "uncensored" W4A16 AWQ weights as the 4090 profile (~18GiB),
# but the 32GB card leaves far more room for KV cache: at 96k context the fp8
# KV cache still reports ~367k tokens of headroom (3.7x concurrency), so the
# context window is raised from 64k to 96k here. It can go higher if you want.
#
# BLACKWELL GOTCHA (handled by native-setup.sh when it detects SM 12.x):
# vLLM hard-requires FlashInfer for this Qwen3.8 GDN hybrid-attention model,
# and FlashInfer JIT-compiles its sm_120 kernels with the *system* nvcc. A
# CUDA < 12.9 toolkit fails with "SM 12.x requires CUDA >= 12.9". native-setup
# installs cuda-toolkit-13-0 and points vLLM at it (CUDA_HOME + arch 12.0).
MODEL_ID=philbert440/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-Aggressive-W4A16-AWQ
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=qwen3.8-27b-uncensored
MAX_MODEL_LEN=98304
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.95
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_coder
REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS="--language-model-only --max-num-seqs 4 --enforce-eager"
